{"engine":"Windows.Media.Ocr en-US","scale":3,"pages":[{"page":1,"width":2436,"height":3156,"lines":[{"text":"OE.SA&","x":339,"y":119,"w":139,"h":48},{"text":"o","x":232,"y":232,"w":25,"h":24},{"text":"OFFICE OF","x":610,"y":154,"w":255,"h":38},{"text":"ASSESSOR-COUNTY CLERK-","x":609,"y":218,"w":699,"h":52},{"text":"RECORDER & ELECTIONS","x":610,"y":294,"w":618,"h":50},{"text":"COUNTY OF SAN MATEO","x":609,"y":373,"w":571,"h":40},{"text":"MARK CHURCH","x":1709,"y":208,"w":385,"h":48},{"text":"CHIEF ELECTIONS OFFICER &","x":1642,"y":271,"w":516,"h":37},{"text":"ASSESSOR-COUNTY CLERK-RECORDER","x":1564,"y":318,"w":675,"h":37},{"text":"Ballot Measure Rebuttal Argument Submission Form","x":550,"y":503,"w":1394,"h":55},{"text":"If both an argument in favor of and an argument against a measure have been selected for publication in the Sample","x":211,"y":586,"w":2046,"h":42},{"text":"Ballot & Official Voter Information Pamphlet, a typed rebuttal to the argument in favor of or the argument against the","x":210,"y":632,"w":2039,"h":41},{"text":"measure may be submitted as outlined in this form.","x":209,"y":680,"w":896,"h":39},{"text":"The author(s) of the primary argument of the measure may prepare and submit a rebuttal argument or may authorize","x":208,"y":756,"w":2050,"h":41},{"text":"in writing any other person or persons to prepare, submit or sign the rebuttal argument.","x":209,"y":803,"w":1522,"h":40},{"text":"A rebuttal argument will not be accepted unless accompanied by this completed form, which shall contain the printed","x":206,"y":880,"w":2048,"h":40},{"text":"name(s) and signature(s) of the person(s) submitting it or, if submitted on behalf of a bona fide association of citizens,","x":208,"y":925,"w":2060,"h":41},{"text":"the name of the association and the printed name and signature of at least one of its principal officers. Please make","x":206,"y":972,"w":2050,"h":39},{"text":"sure you are using proper format before submitting to the Elections Office.","x":206,"y":1017,"w":1411,"h":40},{"text":"Word count limit for Rebuttal Arguments = 250 words","x":205,"y":1095,"w":934,"h":40},{"text":"w","x":483,"y":1163,"w":40,"h":31},{"text":"Ballot Measure","x":206,"y":1174,"w":262,"h":30},{"text":"for the San Mateo Foster City SD to be held on","x":842,"y":1164,"w":908,"h":41},{"text":"11/3/2026","x":1774,"y":1164,"w":173,"h":32},{"text":"C] Rebuttal to Argument in Favor of Measure","x":205,"y":1244,"w":807,"h":52},{"text":"Rebuttal to Argument Against Measure","x":1366,"y":1258,"w":679,"h":40},{"text":"w","x":2065,"y":1248,"w":40,"h":30},{"text":"Signed by Same Individual(s) Selected for the Voter Information Pamphlet for the Primary Argument","x":228,"y":1372,"w":1885,"h":42},{"text":"If the rebuttal argument is signed by the same individual(s) as those already selected for the Voter Information","x":230,"y":1470,"w":1925,"h":41},{"text":"Pamphlet for the primary argument, check the following box and skip the back side of this form.","x":228,"y":1516,"w":1676,"h":42},{"text":"Rebuttal Argument Is Signed by Same Individual(s) Selected for the Voter Information Pamphlet for the","x":351,"y":1585,"w":1806,"h":42},{"text":"Primary Argument","x":351,"y":1632,"w":318,"h":40},{"text":"Contact Person's Printed Name:","x":350,"y":1690,"w":564,"h":33},{"text":"Phone:","x":350,"y":1836,"w":122,"h":32},{"text":"Email:","x":1246,"y":1838,"w":106,"h":31},{"text":"Signed by Different Individual(s) than Individual(s) Selected for the Voter Information Pamphlet for the","x":226,"y":1992,"w":1920,"h":42},{"text":"Primary Argument","x":226,"y":2040,"w":342,"h":38},{"text":"The author(s) of the primary argument may authorize any other person or persons to sign the rebuttal argument. If","x":224,"y":2108,"w":2012,"h":41},{"text":"signers are new for the rebuttal argument, please check the following box, complete the back side of this form and","x":224,"y":2153,"w":1997,"h":41},{"text":"attach the written authorization (the Authorization Form for Change in Signers of Rebuttal Argument) from the","x":224,"y":2200,"w":1916,"h":41},{"text":"primary argument author(s).","x":224,"y":2246,"w":488,"h":40},{"text":"Rebuttal Argument Is Signed by New Signers as Authorized by Primary Argument Author(s)","x":348,"y":2323,"w":1607,"h":41},{"text":"Contact Person's Printed Name:","x":346,"y":2392,"w":563,"h":32},{"text":"Heather Morgan","x":356,"y":2466,"w":284,"h":39},{"text":"Arguments will be emailed to the contact person listed here for review before they are printed in the Sample","x":215,"y":2710,"w":2036,"h":41},{"text":"Ballot & Official Voter Information Pamphlets.","x":804,"y":2756,"w":857,"h":39},{"text":"Please complete the reverse side of this form.","x":802,"y":2826,"w":862,"h":38},{"text":"40 Tower Road, San Mateo, CA 94402","x":860,"y":2881,"w":744,"h":42},{"text":"P 650.312.5222 F 650.312.5348 email registrar@smcacre.gov web www.smcacre.gov","x":378,"y":2934,"w":1709,"h":45}]},{"page":2,"width":2436,"height":3156,"lines":[{"text":"Rebuttal to the Argument Against Measure W","x":767,"y":120,"w":905,"h":44},{"text":"L","x":233,"y":225,"w":55,"h":85},{"text":"We appreciate the generic argument filed by our opponent. This is the same argument this","x":288,"y":262,"w":1754,"h":44},{"text":"group files against all school measures. in our area — regardless of the specific challenges facing","x":288,"y":328,"w":1830,"h":45},{"text":"our schools.","x":287,"y":395,"w":229,"h":36},{"text":"While they're entitled to their opinion, we know that student achievement is rising, not falling.","x":285,"y":529,"w":1829,"h":45},{"text":"Don't take our word for it. We encourage every voter to visit Niche.com, look up the San","x":287,"y":596,"w":1706,"h":45},{"text":"Mateo-Foster City School District, and see that our schools earn an \"A\" rating.","x":286,"y":663,"w":1500,"h":43},{"text":"We also know that our neighborhood schools need urgent repairs to protect quality education","x":284,"y":797,"w":1854,"h":45},{"text":"at a time when State education funding is shrinking and Federal support is disappearing.","x":283,"y":863,"w":1701,"h":46},{"text":"Vote YES on W to keep great teachers in our community at a time when the high cost of living is","x":282,"y":999,"w":1850,"h":43},{"text":"driving teachers away from the Peninsula.","x":282,"y":1065,"w":810,"h":43},{"text":"Vote YES on W to restore vocational programs and shop classes to give our students practical,","x":280,"y":1199,"w":1811,"h":45},{"text":"hands-on skills for future careers.","x":281,"y":1267,"w":644,"h":35},{"text":"Vote YES on W to ensure every student in San Mateo and Foster City has access to a safe","x":278,"y":1402,"w":1712,"h":43},{"text":"classroom that meets modern standards for fire and earthquake safety and access for disabled","x":278,"y":1466,"w":1829,"h":46},{"text":"students — without any remaining lead or asbestos.","x":278,"y":1534,"w":1007,"h":43},{"text":"Vote YES on W to protect strong programs in science, math, literacy, engineering, technology,","x":276,"y":1671,"w":1811,"h":43},{"text":"and career technical education.","x":278,"y":1736,"w":604,"h":36},{"text":"Now is the time to protect OUR local schools. Vote YES on W to secure reliable, local funding for","x":278,"y":1870,"w":1856,"h":46},{"text":"essential, urgent improvements that our teachers and students are counting on.","x":278,"y":1937,"w":1543,"h":46},{"text":"Vote YES on W for great teachers and safe schools!","x":275,"y":2072,"w":983,"h":42},{"text":"FILED","x":1570,"y":2379,"w":94,"h":33},{"text":"OFFICE OF THE CHIEF ELECTIONS OFFICER","x":1256,"y":2422,"w":724,"h":48},{"text":"SAN MATEO","x":1448,"y":2479,"w":192,"h":36},{"text":"7","x":2232,"y":1550,"w":40,"h":51},{"text":"AUG 1 8 2026","x":1497,"y":2587,"w":260,"h":51},{"text":"BY:","x":1259,"y":2788,"w":50,"h":34},{"text":"S OFFICER","x":1808,"y":2702,"w":179,"h":34}]},{"page":3,"width":2436,"height":3156,"lines":[{"text":"Rebuttal Argument Signers Form","x":854,"y":130,"w":62